(5004142, 727285, 96831, '<td valign="top">LOL! Please take no offense here, but this is a ridiculous photo. VERY well shot, looks great. But that outfit and power tools combined cracks me up. I guess this one is more for the ladies. Good work though. :D</td>', 'LOL! Please take no offense here, but this is a ridiculous photo. VERY well shot, looks great. But that outfit and power tools combined cracks me up. I guess this one is more for the ladies. Good work though. :D', '2008-10-11 15:54:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004143, 729137, 96831, '<td valign="top">Seriously? <br/> <br/>What a rare thing to witness though, I must admit.</td>', 'Seriously?  What a rare thing to witness though, I must admit.', '2008-10-11 15:55:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004155, 728967, 83313, '<td valign="top">Yeah, that looks like hard work. What''s he doing? Makes me grateful for a decent paying job that gets some respect. Good colors, but the light is kind of harsh. Biggest thing I would suggest is to change the centered crop of the subject.</td>', 'Yeah, that looks like hard work. What''s he doing? Makes me grateful for a decent paying job that gets some respect. Good colors, but the light is kind of harsh. Biggest thing I would suggest is to change the centered crop of the subject.', '2008-10-11 16:01:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004158, 729156, 83313, '<td valign="top">The whole thing seems soft on detail and slightly OOF, I''m afraid. The idea itself is low on creativity, I think we''ve all done one of these. I know I have, and it got only one comment from my daughter telling me what a geek I am. I think the biggest thing that might help this is to do something to bring out the detail and texture of that sand or soil. (See, I can''t even tell what it is.)</td>', 'The whole thing seems soft on detail and slightly OOF, I''m afraid. The idea itself is low on creativity, I think we''ve all done one of these. I know I have, and it got only one comment from my daughter telling me what a geek I am. I think the biggest thing that might help this is to do something to bring out the detail and texture of that sand or soil. (See, I can''t even tell what it is.)', '2008-10-11 16:06:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004162, 728883, 39110, '<td valign="top">JulirtNN?</td>', 'JulirtNN?', '2008-10-11 16:10:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004164, 728757, 83313, '<td valign="top">Generally, I like this photo, it''s cute and a unique approach. Little kids certainly learn how to "work it" and wrap some grownups around their fingers. Biggest composition problem is the traditional snapshot error of a tree growing out of the subjects head. Probably also, the subject is much too centered in the frame, though that''s debatable as centered comp is sometimes effective.<br/> <br/>The biggest problem, however, is that it seems blurred and unclear. I think most of it is due to the use of excessive JPEG compression. Your file size of only 49k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing most of the detail and sharpness from this image. I can see lots of compression artifacts around the high contrast edges. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)</td>', 'Generally, I like this photo, it''s cute and a unique approach. Little kids certainly learn how to "work it" and wrap some grownups around their fingers. Biggest composition problem is the traditional snapshot error of a tree growing out of the subjects head. Probably also, the subject is much too centered in the frame, though that''s debatable as centered comp is sometimes effective. The biggest problem, however, is that it seems blurred and unclear. I think most of it is due to the use of excessive JPEG compression. Your file size of only 49k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing most of the detail and sharpness from this image. I can see lots of compression artifacts around the high contrast edges. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)', '2008-10-11 16:13:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004169, 727827, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice, but I see lots of compression artifacts in the sky and around the high contrast edges. Your file size of only 53k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing a lot of the detail and sharpness from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)</td>', 'Nice, but I see lots of compression artifacts in the sky and around the high contrast edges. Your file size of only 53k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing a lot of the detail and sharpness from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)', '2008-10-11 16:16:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004173, 728892, 83313, '<td valign="top">I really love the expression here and the idea being conveyed, but the lighting is poor with what looks like the use of an onboard flash. Too bright and slightly washed out close to the camera, and too dark further away. I''ve had some success with bouncing an onboard flash off the ceiling by simply taping a white index card in front of it, angled upward.  How did the doodles score on the SAT?</td>', 'I really love the expression here and the idea being conveyed, but the lighting is poor with what looks like the use of an onboard flash. Too bright and slightly washed out close to the camera, and too dark further away. I''ve had some success with bouncing an onboard flash off the ceiling by simply taping a white index card in front of it, angled upward.  How did the doodles score on the SAT?', '2008-10-11 16:21:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004315, 729172, 2158, '<td valign="top">I wish they were looking down at their work rather than at the camera.</td>', 'I wish they were looking down at their work rather than at the camera.', '2008-10-11 19:21:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5004355, 728202, 40840, '<td valign="top">You may want to crop out the bottom blur, it is distracting.</td>', 'You may want to crop out the bottom blur, it is distracting.', '2008-10-11 20:22:07.000000', NULL, 1),
